      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "When Michael asked you to meet him at an Italian place you happily agreed because you love Italian food. The problem is you informed Michael that you have a gluten allergy and that's when he informed you that he chose the restaurant because their menu has 4 vegetarian dishes and asked you which one you like best. He later left to get a reservation while you were browsing the menu which was when you noticed that 3 out of the 4 vegetarian dishes contain gluten. You then asked Michael how many vegetarian dishes on the menu doesn't contain gluten and he said that the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat is 6 over 10 or 3 over 5.\nSo, how many of the items on the menu can you eat?\n\nTo determine the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat, let's break down the information step by step.\n\n1. **Identify the total number of vegetarian dishes on the menu:**\n   The problem states that there are 4 vegetarian dishes on the menu.\n\n2. **Identify the number of vegetarian dishes that contain gluten:**\n   The problem states that 3 out of the 4 vegetarian dishes contain gluten.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of vegetarian dishes that do not contain gluten:**\n   Since there are 4 vegetarian dishes in total and 3 of them contain gluten, the number of vegetarian dishes that do not contain gluten is:\n   \\[\n   4 - 3 = 1\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat:**\n   The total number of items on the menu is 5 (since 4 vegetarian dishes + 1 meatless dish = 5 items in total). Out of these 5 items, the number that you can eat is 1. Therefore, the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{5}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the fraction of the items on the menu that you can eat is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{5}}\\).",
